(7671443, 1252433, 86447, '<td valign="top">I love this Bear!<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your RIBBON!<br/> <br/>@Wendy:  when a word ends in "s", we just add "es".<br/> <br/>Although, in the cruise port terminal in New Orleans they have a sign every twenty feet or so with "buses" misspelled.  Same signs also have "taxis" misspelled.<br/> <br/>Seems like a bit of Spellcheck would have been in order before they bought a hundred misspelled, huge, metal signs.  *rolleyes*<br/> <br/></td>', 'I love this Bear! Congratulations on your RIBBON! @Wendy:  when a word ends in "s", we just add "es". Although, in the cruise port terminal in New Orleans they have a sign every twenty feet or so with "buses" misspelled.  Same signs also have "taxis" misspelled. Seems like a bit of Spellcheck would have been in order before they bought a hundred misspelled, huge, metal signs.  *rolleyes* ', '2020-08-03 11:00:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7671446, 1252433, 138630, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> I loved this. It was the "buses only" words and arrows that make it.<br/> <br/>(btw, why isn''t the s doubled in the plural!! Shouldn''t it be pronounced "booses"?? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree - the words and arrows add enormously to this one.  <br/>As for buses or busses, the second is an alternate form but archaic and now considered a misspelling by most (according to sources too numerous to mention).  I''m with you on the pronunciation, though, Wendy . . . all I can offer is that it''s for the same reason we don''t rhyme "though" and "rough" . . . no rhyme nor reason, that''s just English :)</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: I loved this. It was the "buses only" words and arrows that make it. (btw, why isn''t the s doubled in the plural!! Shouldn''t it be pronounced "booses"??   I agree - the words and arrows add enormously to this one.  As for buses or busses, the second is an alternate form but archaic and now considered a misspelling by most (according to sources too numerous to mention).  I''m with you on the pronunciation, though, Wendy . . . all I can offer is that it''s for the same reason we don''t rhyme "though" and "rough" . . . no rhyme nor reason, that''s just English :)', '2020-08-03 11:21:06.000000', NULL, 0),
